EVERY MARKER NESTS INSIDE EVERY OTHER, and the host builds one element per pair however deep they
stand: ''b //i ~~s __u ^^sup^^ ,,sub,, __ ~~// ''

A marker opens mid-word: A wo''rd'' here.

Two runs stand adjacent with no text between them: ''one''''two''

A subscript meets a superscript: ,,sub,,^^sup^^

An unclosed run reaches the end of its block and builds NO element — the host needs the pair:
''bold with no closer at all

A marker inside a code span stands as content, because a code span parses nothing: `''not bold''`

